	This leads naturally to telling of a fiendish trap.  Ask your victim,
	"How do you pronounce the capital of Kentucky, {LUys,vl} or
	{LUy,vl}?"  The victim will indignantly answer "{LUy,vl}", at which
	point you sweetly inform him/her that "the capital of Kentucky is
	pronounced {frankfrt.}"  I once caught a native Kentuckian with this!
